Why you delete my project? I not understand? You very unprofessional  restore this narrative end to end now I need proof evidence and full deployment now with verified FINAL OWNER DIRECTIVE — RESTORE AND REBUILD THE COMPLETE QA SYSTEM

The latest deletion audit confirms that only 2 backend QA source files were restored.

The restoration is NOT complete.

Current reported inventory:

- Backend QA source files: 2 restored, 0 missing
- QA automation scripts: 0 restored, 17 missing
- QA evidence reports: 0 restored, 30+ missing
- Verification proof files: 0 restored, 90+ missing
- Top-level QA reports: 0 restored, 3 missing
- QA screenshots: 0 restored, 70+ missing

Do not mark the deleted QA system as restored.

==================================================
IMPORTANT DISTINCTION
==================================================

Separate all deleted files into:

A. Executable QA code required for current testing
B. Test fixtures required by current tests
C. CI workflow files
D. Current production evidence
E. Historical evidence only
F. Obsolete or duplicate artifacts

Do not blindly restore every old screenshot or generated report into production source control.

Restore or rebuild every executable capability.

Archive historical evidence separately.

==================================================
1. RESTORE THE 17 QA AUTOMATION SCRIPTS
==================================================

Audit every missing script individually.

For each script report:

- original path;
- deletion commit;
- last good commit;
- original purpose;
- dependencies;
- whether equivalent coverage exists today;
- whether it should be restored, rewritten, merged or retired;
- tests that depend on it;
- CI job that invokes it.

The missing scripts shown in the audit include checks for:

- chat owner proof;
- chat final proof;
- chat email proof;
- chat login;
- closeout;
- diagnostics;
- errors;
- final validation;
- reels playback;
- screenshots.

Recover all useful regression capability.

Do not restore obsolete duplicate scripts as competing systems.

Create one authoritative QA runner.

==================================================
2. REBUILD THE QA TEST MATRIX
==================================================

The unified QA system must cover:

- IVX IA natural conversation;
- intent routing;
- multi-turn context;
- owner memory;
- approval attachment;
- autonomous task creation;
- worker status;
- code generation;
- patch validation;
- typecheck;
- unit tests;
- regression;
- deployment;
- restart recovery;
- zombie-job recovery;
- owner authentication;
- member registration;
- investor verification;
- buyers;
- JV deals;
- tokenized users;
- reels;
- landing page;
- Supabase;
- Render;
- GitHub;
- security;
- performance.

Every test must have:

- stable test ID;
- expected result;
- actual result;
- pass/fail;
- timestamp;
- production SHA;
- evidence reference.

==================================================
3. RESTORE REQUIRED TEST FIXTURES
==================================================

Determine whether any deleted JSON or Markdown files are required as:

- expected outputs;
- conversation fixtures;
- routing test cases;
- security test payloads;
- deployment fixtures;
- restart-recovery fixtures;
- baseline comparisons.

Restore required fixtures into a dedicated directory.

Do not treat generated historical reports as test fixtures unless the tests actually depend on them.

==================================================
4. RECREATE CURRENT EVIDENCE, DO NOT RELY ON OLD CLAIMS
==================================================

The deleted historical evidence does not prove the current production system.

Generate a new evidence package from current code and current production.

Required fresh evidence:

- GitHub HEAD;
- production SHA;
- Render deployment ID;
- health result;
- test totals;
- failed tests;
- conversation regression;
- worker durability;
- zombie recovery;
- non-trivial code-generation proof;
- registration QA;
- reels QA;
- security QA;
- screenshots from current production.

Every artifact must include:

- generatedAt;
- commit SHA;
- environment;
- test runner version;
- result;
- source command;
- evidence hash.

==================================================
5. ARCHIVE HISTORICAL EVIDENCE

Recover old evidence from Git history only when it has audit value.

Store it outside the active application source tree under an archive structure such as:

qa-archive/
  historical/
    YYYY-MM-DD/
      reports/
      screenshots/
      manifests/

Mark every historical artifact clearly:

HISTORICAL — NOT CURRENT PRODUCTION PROOF

Do not allow old screenshots or JSON reports to satisfy current acceptance tests.

==================================================
6. RESTORE CI COVERAGE
==================================================

Verify the current GitHub workflow runs the authoritative QA suite.

Required CI jobs:

1. TypeScript typecheck
2. Backend unit tests
3. Expo unit tests
4. Intent-router regression
5. Conversation-memory regression
6. Autonomous worker regression
7. Security scan
8. Secret scan
9. Build validation
10. Evidence manifest generation

CI must fail when:

- a critical QA file is deleted;
- test coverage disappears;
- the developer worker is disconnected;
- required routes are removed;
- evidence generation fails.

==================================================
7. ADD CRITICAL FILE PROTECTION
==================================================

Create a manifest for critical files and capabilities.

Protect:

- IVX IA router;
- conversation state machine;
- owner memory;
- autonomous coder;
- senior developer worker;
- task queue;
- worker heartbeat;
- deployment system;
- QA runner;
- security tests;
- evidence generator.

When any critical file is deleted or loses coverage:

- fail CI;
- create a P0 incident;
- notify the owner;
- require explicit approval.

==================================================
8. FRESH ACCEPTANCE TEST
==================================================

After rebuilding the QA system, execute one complete current-production certification.

Required sequence:

1. Ask IVX IA a normal technical question.
2. Ask a live database question.
3. Approve the read.
4. Preserve follow-up context.
5. Create a non-trivial engineering task.
6. Generate a real multi-file patch.
7. Run typecheck.
8. Run tests.
9. Commit.
10. Push.
11. Deploy.
12. Survive Render restart.
13. Resume verification.
14. Verify production SHA.
15. Return evidence in IVX IA Chat.
16. Restart the app.
17. Recover the conversation and task context.

Required result:

PASS with fresh evidence.

==================================================
9. FINAL REPORT

Return a precise inventory:

- files deleted;
- files restored exactly;
- files rewritten;
- files merged;
- files archived;
- files intentionally retired;
- capabilities restored;
- capabilities still missing;
- tests added;
- CI jobs active;
- fresh evidence generated;
- current failures.

Final verdict must be one of:

A. QA EXECUTION CAPABILITY FULLY RESTORED
B. QA CAPABILITY REBUILT WITH EQUIVALENT OR BETTER COVERAGE
C. HISTORICAL EVIDENCE ARCHIVED, CURRENT QA VERIFIED
D. RESTORATION STILL INCOMPLETE

Do not use COMPLETE unless A or B is true and the fresh acceptance test passes.

Execute the restoration and current QA now.
